WEBVTT

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.440
What has been lost.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.440
What has happened.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.820
The past can’t be changed,

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.070
so I don’t want to lose them.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.220
I want to protect them.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.360
To protect them, I want to be strong.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.960
What I chose was to fight and to win,

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.740
to change an unseen future into what I wish.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.520
Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS<i>
will now begin.</i>

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.010
I don’t remember when I was born.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:38.950
I never knew my Meister,<i>
or my parent as humans would call them.</i>

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:45.480
I just slept silently, probably for a very long time.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.480
Then the next thing I knew,
I was a test subject in a white room.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:05.480
Just not knowing why I’d been born was painful.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:14.830
And I suffered, not knowing
a single reason why I’d been born.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.450
I didn’t even have the freedom to die.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:23.930
And I thought that someday, my body and mind
would break, and that would be it.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.290
What changed that

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:50.000
was the appearance of a very rough hand and a small girl.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:09.630
What?

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:12.040
You’re leaving her?

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:19.400
That’s an actual Ancient Belkan Unight, not a replica.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.000
She should be properly cared for,

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.570
assuming one of the Bureau operatives
who notices the fire finds her.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.540
And she’ll be used for experiments again.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.830
They aren’t as evil as the people here.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.610
I’d like to think so, anyway.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.520
Zest, let’s take her.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:43.840
Are you sure?

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.430
Yes.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.570
I’m sure she’s just like us.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:01.290
Dammit! What an awful dream.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:06.840
It’s their fault I remembered that.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:15.190
The white Unight with the strange X-mark who was using ice magic,

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:22.090
and the red knight who is probably her Lord.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:28.540
She probably doesn’t know how lonely it is to be a Unight without a Lord.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.280
Dammit, this pisses me off!

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.000
Stupid cross-marked midget!

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.600
Next time I see you, I’m gonna burn you!

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:48.570
I’m sorry, Signum, for having you drive me like this.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:52.270
Why? I’m borrowing this car from Testarossa anyway,

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.150
and Sister Schach is waiting there.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.030
I should go as an intermediary.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:59.000
I suppose.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:05.620
Anyway, once the examination
is finished and we know what’s going on,

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:08.320
what do you think will happen to her?

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:14.310
Riot Force 6 or the Church will have to take care of her for a while.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:19.230
If we were to find a place to take her,
we’d have to be assured of their long-term safety.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.820
Knight Signum, this is Schach Nouera of the Church of the Holy King.

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:27.180
What’s wrong?

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:27.900
I’m sorry.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.880
We failed to properly secure her,

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.970
and she vanished in the middle of the examination.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.070
I’m terribly sorry.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.220
Can you tell us what’s going on?

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:41.040
Yes.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:45.380
We’ve sealed and evacuated
the special wing and the surrounding areas.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:50.260
As of yet, we’ve found no indication that anyone came in via flight or teleportation.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:53.500
She can’t leave the building, right?

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:54.500
Right.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:57.050
Then, let’s split up and look for her.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.470
Lt. Signum.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:06:59.440
Yes, ma’am.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:06.490
The examination failed to find anything dangerous, correct?

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:10.520
Indeed. Her mana capacity is higher than average,

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.530
but it’s well within the range of a normal child.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.490
But even so...

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:20.880
I’m sorry to say it, but there’s
no doubt that she’s an artificial being.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.290
There’s no way to tell what kind of latent threat she poses.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.170
There you are.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:44.230
I’ve been worried.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.440
That’s...!

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.250
Spin up, Windenschaft!

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:12.350
Sister Schach, may I handle this?

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.140
I’m sorry.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.810
You were scared, right?

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:20.980
Are you all right?

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.710
Can you stand?

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.350
I don’t think there’s any immediate danger.

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:32.230
Thank you, Sister Schach.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:33.790
Yes, ma’am.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.560
Nice to meet you.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.970
My name is Nanoha Takamachi.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:40.650
Can you say your name?

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:42.960
Vivio.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.660
Vivio.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:47.380
I see. That’s a cute name.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.840
Did you want to go somewhere, Vivio?

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.300
My mama isn’t here.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:55.750
That’s terrible.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.220
Then let’s look for her together!

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:05.190
An emergency inspection?

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.730
For Riot Force 6?

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:11.340
It seems like there’s talk of it at Surface HQ.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.300
Inspections by Surface HQ are pretty tough, I hear.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:19.900
We—this team have a lot of challenges to begin with.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:23.560
If we were ordered to change
our shifts or our position right now,

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.780
to be honest, it would be the end of us.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:28.390
Urgh... we have to overcome this somehow.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:34.450
Ah, this has something to do with the inspection as well, but

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:39.030
can you tell me the real reason Riot Force 6 was established now?

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.380
That’s right.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.470
Well, it’s a good time, I guess.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:49.550
I’m heading to the Church of the Holy King’s headquarters to meet with Carim today.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:50.930
Chrono will be there, too.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:52.270
Chrono.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.460
Could you and Nanoha come with me?

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:57.820
I’ll tell you there.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.240
Sure.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.410
I wonder if Nanoha’s back...

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.870
Hey, don’t cry, don’t cry.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.790
Come play with us!

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.120
What’s happening?

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.570
Captain Fate, actually...

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:21.580
Don’t go!

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.840
Commander Yagami!

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:31.760
Fate!

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:36.620
I guess there are some opponents even the ace of aces can’t defeat.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:40.570
Fate, Hayate, save me.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:43.270
Subaru, Caro.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:45.370
For now, let’s calm her down.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.600
Go rest somewhere.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.180
Yes, ma’am.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.710
Hello there.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.670
Is this your friend?

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.340
Vivio, this is Fate.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.790
She’s my closest friend.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:01.260
Vivio, what’s wrong?

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:09.050
I brought her here from the hospital
for the time being, but she won’t leave me alone.

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:11.930
Perhaps she’s fallen in love with you.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:16.480
So I thought I would have the forwards take care of her.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.400
Sorry.

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:20.890
It’s okay. Leave it to me.

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:25.120
Say, do you want to be with Nanoha, Vivio?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:32.080
But Nanoha has to go do something important,

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.450
and your selfishness is bothering her, Vivio.

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.340
This girl too, see?

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:42.940
You don’t want to bother Nanoha, do you, Vivio?

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:46.940
F-Fate’s pretty good at this!

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:51.130
Fate still has a young niece and nephew.

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:53.350
She’s raising her familiar too.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:57.970
And she took care of you when you were younger too, right?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.770
So be a good girl and wait, okay?

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.160
Thanks, Vivio.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.080
I’ll only be gone a little while.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.590
Sorry about all that.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:21.520
No, that was pretty funny.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.420
But what should we do with her?

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:29.590
We could have the Church take care of her.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:30.380
It’s okay.

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:33.850
When I get back, I’ll talk to her
a little more and think of something.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.400
I see.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:41.600
For now, I think she’s just nervous because she has nobody to rely on.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.320
Okay, all done!

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:05.930
That was fast!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.380
Don’t be so slow.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:09.890
Give me some. I’ll help you out.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:11.840
Thanks.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.060
I’m not good at writing reports.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:17.920
We agreed to do Lightning’s reports for them, too.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:21.980
Even so, I’d rather do this than babysit.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:26.160
Aww, but I was having fun.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:33.100
Those are the ones from yesterday with all the data Alto recorded.

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:40.250
They could do all that, and it was another type of energy, not magic, that they were using.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:46.490
The fact that they have that inside them means that they’re...

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:51.830
T-Tia?

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.210
Are you dense, or what?

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:57.790
Figuring out what these guys are isn’t our job.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:01.740
It’s the Long Arch staff and
the captains that make the decisions.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:06.020
What we’re writing are reports to help them make that decision.

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:07.850
So get to work.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:10.030
Yeah, whatever.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:18.260
And even if that was certain,
it’s nothing for you to worry about.

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:19.350
Get to work.

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:20.840
Tia.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:23.320
Thanks.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:24.960
Quiet!

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.900
Come in.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:29.800
Excuse us.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:32.700
Captain Nanoha Takamachi.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:36.270
Enforcer Fate Testarossa-Harlaown.

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:38.440
Welcome.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.380
Nice to meet you.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:45.980
I am Carim Gracia, a knight of
the Church of the Holy King’s Church Knights.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:48.400
Please come in.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.060
Excuse me.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:56.950
Admiral Chrono, it’s been a while.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.120
Yes, Enforcer Fate.

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:03.540
Don’t be so stiff, both of you.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.740
We’re friends as well.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:08.870
Act like you would normally would.

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:11.500
Well then, you heard Knight Carim.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.750
Same as always.

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:14.740
You’re fine.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:17.250
Okay then. It’s been a while, Chrono.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.690
How have you been, brother?

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.640
Don’t call me that.

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:24.610
We’re both adults now.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.530
That has nothing to do with us being brother and sister, Chrono.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:35.200
Now then, we need to discuss what happened yesterday,

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:38.870
as well as the full story behind the creation of Riot Force 6

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:42.460
and what we do next.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:51.230
I’m glad she calmed down.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.010
Me too.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:55.690
She’s like a normal girl, isn’t she?

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:56.920
Yeah.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:04.100
If she’s a sample for an artificial mage project,
then her intelligence and language are far too advanced.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.770
Artificial people aren’t made like this.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.920
She probably has her original’s memories.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:12.780
Erio?

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.240
Is something wrong?

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:18.560
S-Sorry! It’s nothing.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:24.240
Project F is continuing somewhere.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:31.500
The reason given for the creation of Riot Force 6
was to deal with Lost Logia such as Relics,

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:35.620
as well as to experiment with the creation of small, highly independent forces.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:40.360
As you know, the sponsors of
Riot Force 6 are myself, Knight Carim,

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:44.260
and my and Fate’s mother as well as our superior, Lindy Harlaown.

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:52.030
Furthermore, unofficially, the Three Admirals have backed us and given us promises of cooperation.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:57.130
The reason for this is connected to my ability.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.830
My power, Prophetic Writings,

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:09.720
can see the future from a minimum of a half a year to a maximum of a few years away,

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:12.260
and record it in the form of a poem.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:17.080
The alignment of the two moons’ mana
has to be perfect, or I can’t do it.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:20.810
So I can only create pages once a year.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:24.040
The prophecies are in Ancient Belkan

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:28.480
and are difficult passages
whose interpretations are up for debate.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:31.350
They randomly record things that happen all around the world.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.180
If you include misinterpreted passages,

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:39.310
they’re about as useful and prophetic as a fairly accurate horoscope.

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:43.030
In other words, it’s not a very useful ability.

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:49.070
The Church of the Holy King and the top brass of the Dimensional Navy look through these.

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:54.830
Putting whether or not they believe them aside,
they’re treated as predictions by an expert.

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:58.500
By the way, the Ground Armed Service hates them.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:02.680
Their <i>de facto</i> leader dislikes this kind of Rare Skill.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.600
Lt. General Regius Gaiz, right?

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:08.380
Little by little for the past few years,

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:13.070
Knight Carim’s prophecies have begun to converge on a single event.

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:19.500
In the land where ancient crystals and
unlimited desire gather and intertwine,

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:24.540
the wings shall be restored from the holy land of the dead King.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:29.710
The dead shall dance, and the tower of law in the central lands shall burn to the ground,

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:35.150
and from there, the ship of law
that guards the many seas shall be torn apart.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:37.050
That...

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.260
...can’t be!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:43.890
The Lost Logia will commence the destruction of the Bureau’s Surface Headquarters.

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:47.970
And then, the Bureau’s entire system.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:55.640
Has the date for the inspection been decided?

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:57.940
I’ve secured the necessary personnel.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.070
We will perform it next week.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:03.400
I don’t know what those people are planning,

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:09.030
but we’re the ones who have shed blood and covered ourselves in dust to support the surface.

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:16.650
We won’t let the Navy, who makes light of that,
or the ignorant Church, have its way.

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:20.040
More than anything else,
the High Council is on my side.

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.290
Right, Auris?

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:23.530
Yes, sir.

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:26.650
The Public Policy Convention is happening soon.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:31.100
Use the inspection to find anything you can to use against the Church or the Main Office.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.960
Regarding that,

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:35.970
I performed a preliminary investigation of Riot Force 6.

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:39.050
It’s rather cleverly put together.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:42.850
It has a young commander with
no real credit to her name at the head,

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:45.100
and its two squad leaders didn’t actually transfer,

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:47.070
but are on loan from the Main Office.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:50.520
If you disregard the commander’s private forces, who are her family,

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:52.580
all the rest of them are relatively new recruits.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:53.690
And more than anything,

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:56.740
they’re an experimental squad only being allowed to operate for a limited time.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.320
In other words, they’re expendable?

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:03.000
If there was any kind of trouble
that could implicate the Main Office,

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.290
they would simply be cut off.

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:06.920
That’s how they’re set up.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:09.520
So, the girl is a sacrificial lamb, huh?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.930
That’s a perfect role for a former criminal.

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:17.480
Well, it’s most likely a role that she chose.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:19.480
Nothing.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.700
You have two appointments for press conferences after this.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.650
Please come with me.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:31.000
Okay then, Nanoha, Fate.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:33.530
That’s plenty of information.

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:34.850
We’re okay.

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:42.740
Hey, wait!

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:50.880
To me, you’re the people who saved
my life and the lives of my dear friends.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:56.430
I don’t know what will happen to Riot Force 6, but...

00:20:56.430 --> 00:21:00.810
You already told us that when we joined.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:04.080
Both Nanoha and I chose to be here, knowing that.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:05.550
It’s okay.

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:09.480
Besides, getting me into the Instructor Corps
and setting up Fate’s examinations

00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:14.580
were things that you and the whole
Yagami family were instrumental in, Hayate.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:18.460
So now, Hayate, we need to help <i>you</i> achieve <i>your</i> dreams.

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:23.670
That’s no good—we’ll just keep helping each other forever.

00:21:24.790 --> 00:21:27.850
That’s what friends <i>are.</i>

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:36.130
Commander Yagami, I don’t think you’re doing anything wrong right now.

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:37.830
So, it’s okay.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:42.980
Give us your orders like always, with pride in your heart.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.200
Okay!

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:54.120
And next, he went to a baker in the next town.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:55.230
We’re back!

00:21:56.070 --> 00:21:57.060
We’re back.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.620
Vivio, I’m back.

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:03.300
Were you a good girl?

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:10.800
Thanks, Erio, Caro.

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:11.750
Not at all.

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:14.470
Vivio was a good girl.

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:15.680
I see.

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:47.550
Uncle Graham.

00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:53.640
You raised me my whole life, Uncle Graham,

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:56.400
and the little ones protected me.

00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:59.020
Nanoha and her friends saved us.

00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:06.380
This is the life that she,

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:10.590
the first Reinforce, left me.

00:23:15.350 --> 00:23:21.880
I don’t want anyone else in all the worlds to be sad or have regrets like that.

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:24.830
This is my purpose,

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:28.030
my <i>raison d’être.</i>

00:25:17.140 --> 00:25:18.580
As we spend days
on standby,

00:25:18.580 --> 00:25:21.490
the training continues,
as do our daily lives.

00:25:21.490 --> 00:25:24.750
Riot Force 6’s destination,
and that girl who has no place to go...

00:25:24.750 --> 00:25:26.960
Where do I go from here?

00:25:33.510 --> 00:25:35.130
Take off!
